IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`
IMPORT `euca-s203-indicators`

-- Tests for section 203(d), (e), (f): the State "on" and "off" indicators.
-- Every expected value below was worked out by hand from the text of the Act before the file was
-- run; each case says what the hand calculation was. Rates are percentage points.
-- Weeks are dates on which a week begins. Nothing here is a rule of the Act.

§ `Tests: the indicators of section 203(d), (e), (f)`

§§ `203(e): the rate of insured unemployment`

-- 5 claimants a week on average, 100 covered: 5 / 100 = 5 per cent.
#ASSERT (`the rate of insured unemployment` 5 100) EQUALS JUST 5
-- 0 covered employment cannot be divided by: the rate is NOTHING (a fork: the text is silent).
#ASSERT (`the rate of insured unemployment` 5 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 3 / 40 = 0.075, i.e. 7.5 per cent.
#ASSERT (`the rate of insured unemployment` 3 40) EQUALS JUST 7.5

-- s 203(d), last sentence: the first four of the six quarters, 100 200 300 400 are averaged: 250.
#ASSERT (`the average monthly covered employment for a thirteen-week period` (LIST 100, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600)) EQUALS JUST 250
-- Five quarters are not six: the text names the first four of the most recent SIX.
#ASSERT (`the average monthly covered employment for a thirteen-week period` (LIST 100, 200, 300, 400, 500)) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `203(d)(1): the State on indicator, the 120 per cent and 5 per cent tests`

-- A State law that has adopted neither option; the preceding two years' rates are both 4.
`in the indicator tests, a reading with no option` MEANS
    `Insured unemployment reading` WITH
        `rate of insured unemployment for the week and the preceding twelve weeks` IS 5
        `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the first preceding calendar year` IS 4
        `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the second preceding calendar year` IS 4
        `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the third preceding calendar year` IS 0
        `date from which the State law adopts the 6 per cent option` IS NOTHING
        `date from which the State law adopts the three-year comparison option` IS NOTHING

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
      first IS A NUMBER
      second IS A NUMBER
      third IS A NUMBER
      sixOption IS A MAYBE DATE
      threeYearOption IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `Insured unemployment reading`
`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` rate first second third sixOption threeYearOption MEANS
    `Insured unemployment reading` WITH
        `rate of insured unemployment for the week and the preceding twelve weeks` IS rate
        `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the first preceding calendar year` IS first
        `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the second preceding calendar year` IS second
        `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the third preceding calendar year` IS third
        `date from which the State law adopts the 6 per cent option` IS sixOption
        `date from which the State law adopts the three-year comparison option` IS threeYearOption

-- 5 against two years of 4 and 4: 120 per cent of 4 is 4.8; 5 is at least 4.8 and at least 5. ON.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 6 1 2013) `in the indicator tests, a reading with no option`
-- 4.9 is 120 per cent of 4 or more (4.8) but is below 5: not ON, so OFF.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 4.9 4 4 0 NOTHING NOTHING)
-- 5.9 against 5 and 5: 120 per cent of 5 is 6; 5.9 falls short: OFF though above 5.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 5.9 5 5 0 NOTHING NOTHING)
-- 6 against 5 and 5: exactly 120 per cent ("equaled or exceeded"): ON.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 5 5 0 NOTHING NOTHING)
-- Two years are averaged: (4 + 6) / 2 = 5, 120 per cent of that is 6; a rate of 6 is ON.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 4 6 0 NOTHING NOTHING)
-- The third year is not read without the option: (4 + 4) / 2 = 4, so 5 is ON whatever the third year was.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 5 4 4 50 NOTHING NOTHING)

§§ `203(d), closing paragraph: the 6 per cent option`

-- Option adopted from 1 January 2011: for the week of 1 March 2011 the rate need only be 6.
-- 6 against 5 and 5 would be ON anyway; the discriminating case is 6 against 10 and 10 (120 per cent is 12).
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 1 3 2011) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 10 10 0 (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)) NOTHING)
-- The same facts with no option: 6 is below 12: OFF.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 1 3 2011) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 10 10 0 NOTHING NOTHING)
-- The option still needs 6: 5.9 is OFF.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 1 3 2011) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 5.9 10 10 0 (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)) NOTHING)
-- The option reaches "weeks beginning after March 30, 1977": an option adopted in 1975 starts on the later date.
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law's 6 per cent option applies to the week` (Date 30 3 1977) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 10 10 0 (JUST (Date 1 1 1975)) NOTHING))
#ASSERT `the State law's 6 per cent option applies to the week` (Date 31 3 1977) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 10 10 0 (JUST (Date 1 1 1975)) NOTHING)
-- An option adopted later than 1977 starts after the date the State law establishes: the day itself is not after it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law's 6 per cent option applies to the week` (Date 1 1 2011) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 10 10 0 (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)) NOTHING))
#ASSERT `the State law's 6 per cent option applies to the week` (Date 2 1 2011) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 10 10 0 (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)) NOTHING)
-- A week that is ON under paragraph (1) stays ON under the option: 10 against 5 and 5 is ON with or without it.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 1 3 2011) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 10 5 5 0 (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)) NOTHING)

§§ `203(d), closing paragraph: the three-year option`

-- Option from 1 January 2011. A rate of 6 against years of 5, 5 and 8:
--   two years: (5 + 5) / 2 = 5, 120 per cent is 6, so 6 is ON;  three years: (5 + 5 + 8) / 3 = 6, 120 per cent is 7.2, so 6 is OFF.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 5 5 8 NOTHING NOTHING)
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(d)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 5 5 8 NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)))
-- The option covers weeks "ending on or before December 31, 2013": a week beginning 25 December 2013 ends 31 December: covered.
#ASSERT `the State law's three-year comparison option of section 203(d) applies to the week` (Date 25 12 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 5 5 8 NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)))
-- A week beginning 26 December 2013 ends 1 January 2014: not covered.
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law's three-year comparison option of section 203(d) applies to the week` (Date 26 12 2013) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 5 5 8 NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 1 2011))))
-- An option date earlier than 17 December 2010 is replaced by that date: a week beginning on it is not "after" it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law's three-year comparison option of section 203(d) applies to the week` (Date 17 12 2010) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 5 5 8 NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 1 2010))))
#ASSERT `the State law's three-year comparison option of section 203(d) applies to the week` (Date 18 12 2010) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 6 5 5 8 NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 1 2010)))

§§ `203(f): the alternative trigger on total unemployment`

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
      first IS A NUMBER
      second IS A NUMBER
      third IS A NUMBER
      adopted IS A BOOLEAN
      threeYearOption IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Total unemployment reading`
`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` rate first second third adopted threeYearOption MEANS
    `Total unemployment reading` WITH
        `average rate of total unemployment (seasonally adjusted) for the most recent 3 months for which data for all States are published` IS rate
        `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the first preceding calendar year` IS first
        `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the second preceding calendar year` IS second
        `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the third preceding calendar year` IS third
        `the State law adopts the alternative trigger` IS adopted
        `date from which the State law adopts the three-year comparison option` IS threeYearOption

-- 6.5 against 5 and 5: clause (i) is met (6.5 equals 6.5), clause (ii) is met (110 per cent of 5 is 5.5): ON.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 6.5 5 5 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- 6.4 falls below 6.5: not ON; the State is "off" under (B) since the trigger applies.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 6.4 5 5 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- Clause (ii) unmet: 7 against 7 and 7: 110 per cent of 7 is 7.7, 7 is below it: OFF though above 6.5.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 7 7 7 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- "either (or both)": 11 against 20 and 10: 110 per cent of 10 is 11, which 11 equals: ON by the second year only.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 20 10 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- 11 against 10 and 20: ON by the first year only.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 10 20 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- 10.9 against 10 and 10 is below 11: OFF.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 10.9 10 10 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- The State has not adopted the trigger: neither ON nor OFF by (f).
#ASSERT NOT (`there is a State on indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 10 10 0 FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`there is a State off indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 10 10 0 FALSE NOTHING))
-- "beginning after March 6, 1993": the week of 6 March 1993 is outside; 7 March 1993 is inside.
#ASSERT NOT (`the alternative trigger applies to the week` (Date 6 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 10 10 0 TRUE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `the alternative trigger applies to the week` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 10 10 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- Three-year option, from 1 January 2011: 11 against 20, 20 and 10 is ON only through the third year.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 20 20 10 TRUE (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)))
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 20 20 10 TRUE NOTHING)
-- After 31 December 2013 the option is spent: the week beginning 26 December 2013 ends in 2014.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator under section 203(f)` (Date 26 12 2013) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 11 20 20 10 TRUE (JUST (Date 1 1 2011)))

§§ `203(f), last sentence: a week that is ON under (d) stays ON`

-- A State on indicator under (d) (5 against 4 and 4) with the trigger adopted but its test failing (3 against 3, 3): ON.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator for the week` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, a reading with no option`) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 3 3 3 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- ON by (f) alone (insured test 4.9 fails): ON.
#ASSERT `there is a State on indicator for the week` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 4.9 4 4 0 NOTHING NOTHING) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 6.5 5 5 0 TRUE NOTHING)
-- Neither: OFF.
#ASSERT `there is a State off indicator for the week` (Date 7 3 1993) (`in the indicator tests, an insured unemployment reading of` 4.9 4 4 0 NOTHING NOTHING) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 6.4 5 5 0 TRUE NOTHING)

§§ `203(f)(1)(A) at 8 per cent (the percentage section 202(b)(3)(B) substitutes)`

-- 8 against 7 and 7: 8 equals 8 and 110 per cent of 7 is 7.7: met.
#ASSERT `the alternative trigger test is met at the percentage` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 8 7 7 0 FALSE NOTHING) 8
-- 7.9 falls below 8: not met, though it would be met at 6.5.
#ASSERT NOT (`the alternative trigger test is met at the percentage` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 7.9 7 7 0 FALSE NOTHING) 8)
#ASSERT `the alternative trigger test is met at the percentage` (Date 6 1 2013) (`in the indicator tests, a total unemployment reading of` 7.9 7 7 0 FALSE NOTHING) 6.5

§§ `The people who decide`

#ASSERT `the party who makes the determinations under subsection (d)` EQUALS `the State agency`
#ASSERT `the party who determines the rate of total unemployment and any seasonal adjustment` EQUALS `the Secretary of Labor`
